-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Demographic surveillance sites and emerging challenges in international health</article-title><source>Bull World Health Organ</source><volume>84</volume><fpage>163</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16583067</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0050057-b023"><citation citation-type="other"><collab>Data Documentation Initiative</collab><year>2007</year><article-title>About the specification</article-title><comment>Available: <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.ddialliance.org/codebook/index.html">http://www.ddialliance.org/codebook/index.html</ext-link>. Accessed 29 January 2008</comment></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0050057-b024"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group><name><surname>Lowrance</surname><given-names>WW</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Access to collections of data and materials for health research: A report to the MRC and the Wellcome Trust</article-title><comment>Available: <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.wellcome.ac.uk/doc_WTX030843.html">http://www.wellcome.ac.uk/doc_WTX030843.html</ext-link>. Accessed 29 January 2008</comment></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0050057-b025"><citation citation-type="other"><collab>INDEPTH Network</collab><year>2005</year><article-title>Publications from INDEPTH</article-title><comment>Available: <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.indepth-network.org/publications/indepth_publications.htm">http://www.indepth-network.org/publications/indepth_publications.htm</ext-link>. Accessed 29 January 2008</comment></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0050057-b026"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Ezzati</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Lopez</surname><given-names>AD</given-names></name><name><surname>Rodgers</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Murray</surname><given-names>CJL</given-names></name></person-group><comment>editors</comment><year>2004</year><source>Comparative quantification of health risks: Global and regional burden of diseases attributable to selected major risk factors</source><publisher-loc>Geneva</publisher-loc><publisher-name>World Health Organization</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0050057-b027"><citation citation-type="other"><collab>World Health Organization</collab><year>2002</year><article-title>The world health report 2002: Reducing risks, promoting healthy life</article-title><comment>Available: <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.who.int/whr/2002">http://www.who.int/whr/2002</ext-link>. Accessed 29 January 2008</comment></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0050057-b028"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group><name><surname>&#x000dc;st&#x000fc;n</surname><given-names>TB</given-names></name><name><surname>Chatterji</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Villanueva</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Bendib</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>&#x000c7;elik</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>WHO multi-country survey study on health and responsiveness 2000&#x02013;2001. World Health Organization</article-title><comment>Available: <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.who.int/healthinfo/survey/whspaper37.pdf">http://www.who.int/healthinfo/survey/whspaper37.pdf</ext-link>. Accessed 29 January 2008</comment></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0050057-b029"><citation citation-type="other"><collab>World Health Organizatoni</collab><year>2007</year><article-title>World health survey</article-title><comment>Available: <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.who.int/healthinfo/survey/en/">http://www.who.int/healthinfo/survey/en/</ext-link>. Accessed 29 January 2008</comment></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0050057-b030"><citation citation-type="book"><collab>World Health Organization</collab><year>2007</year><source>Verbal autopsy standards: Ascertaining and attributing cause of death</source><publisher-loc>Geneva</publisher-loc><publisher-name>World Health Organization</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0050057-b031"><citation citation-type="other"><collab>Health Metrics Network</collab><year>2007</year><article-title>Stepping stones to improving the monitoring of vital events: A resource kit for strengthening national vital statistics systems</article-title><comment>Available: <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.who.int/healthmetrics/tools/logbook/en/move/web/index.html">http://www.who.int/healthmetrics/tools/logbook/en/move/web/index.html</ext-link>. Accessed 29 January 2008</comment></citation></ref></ref-list><fn-group><fn id="n3" fn-type="current-aff"><p>Daniel Chandramohan and Sandy Cairncross are in the Department of Infectious and Tropical Diseases, London School of Hygiene and Tropical Medicine, London, United Kingdom. E-mail: <email>Daniel.chandramohan&#x00040;lshtm.ac.uk</email> and <email>sandy.cairncross&#x00040;</email> lshtm.ac.uk. Kenji Shibuya is the Coordinator of the Health Statistics and Evidence Unit, Measurement and Health Information Systems, World Health Organization, Geneva, Switzerland. E-mail: <email>shibuyak&#x00040;who.int</email>. Philip Setel is at MEASURE Evaluation/Carolina Population Center, and the Departments of Epidemiology and Anthropology, University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill, Chapel Hill, North Carolina, United States of America. E-mail: <email>psetel&#x00040;unc.edu</email>. Alan D. Lopez is at the School of Population Health, University of Queensland, Brisbane, Queensland, Australia. E-mail: <email>a.lopez&#x00040;sph.uq.edu.au</email>. Christopher J. L. Murray is at the Institute for Health Metrics and Evaluation, University of Washington, Seattle, Washington, United States of America. E-mail: <email>cjlm&#x00040;u.washington.edu</email>. Basia &#x0017b;aba is at the National Institute for Medical Research, Mwanza, Tanzania and the Department of Epidemiology and Population Health, London School of Hygiene and Tropical Medicine, London, United Kingdom. E-mail: <email>Basia.Zaba&#x00040;lshtm.ac.uk</email>. Robert W. Snow is at the Centre for Geographic Medicine, Kenya Medical Research Institute&#x02013;University of Oxford&#x02013;Wellcome Trust Collaborative Programme, Nairobi, Kenya. E-mail: <email>rsnow&#x00040;nairobi.kemri-wellcome.org</email>. Fred Binka is at the INDEPTH Network, Accra, Ghana. E-mail: <email>fred.binka&#x00040;indepth-network.org</email></p></fn><fn id="n1" fn-type="financial-disclosure"><p><bold>Funding:</bold> The authors received no specific funding for this article.</p></fn><fn id="n2" fn-type="conflict"><p><bold>Competing Interests:</bold> Basia &#x0017b;aba is Principal Investigator of the Alpha network of DSS sites specializing in HIV research (the network facilitates joint data analyses). Fred Binka is on the staff of the INDEPTH Network secretariat supporting DSS sites in the developing world. The remaining authors have declared that no competing interests exist.</p></fn></fn-group></back></article>